        "original_id": "baab05b4-e682-5350-a71a-f8352c6886bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Waris Hussein, Mathieu Kassovitz, Shirley MacLaine, Perry King\n- Works: Doctor Who, Play of the Month, A Passage to India, Amélie, The Possession of Joel Delaney\n- Roles: television director, film director, director, screenwriter, producer, editor, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Waris Hussein was born on 9 December 1938 and is a British-Indian television director and film director.\n- In 1965, Waris Hussein directed the Play of the Month version of A Passage to India.\n- Waris Hussein is best known for British television productions including Doctor Who.\n- The Possession of Joel Delaney is a 1972 American horror film directed by Waris Hussein and starring Shirley MacLaine and Perry King.\n- Mathieu Kassovitz was born on 3 August 1967 and is a French director, screenwriter, producer, editor, and actor.\n- In Francophone countries, Mathieu Kassovitz is probably best known for playing Nino Quincampoix in Amélie (Le Fabuleux Destin d'Amélie Poulain), released in 2001.",
